 "relevance_note": "This cohort deep-sequencing study gives individual-level detail for three patients with mosaic TNFAIP3 variants: \"had mosaic variants in TNFAIP3\" (Patient IDs 66, 99, 507), so individuals with a TNFAIP3 variant are reported.",
 "method_note": "Read only the paper, the schema, the rules and the instructions; built the JSON by hand from verbatim table cells (Table 1 and Table 3) and text sentences, then checked every span against the paper Markdown with a grep-style search. Scope: only the three patients with a TNFAIP3 variant (Patient IDs 66, 99, 507) are in scope; the other 449 affected and 154 healthy cohort members (including those with mosaic variants in FAS, STAT3, NRAS, UBA1 and other genes, and the unaffected mother with a STAT3 p.Thr389Ser variant) are out of scope and get no rows. Labels: the paper prints these patients as \"Patient ID 66\", \"Patient 66\" or bare table values (\"66\"); the most common text form (\"Patient ID\") was used. Variant type for Patient ID 507 is taken from the \"Frameshift\" class heading of his row in Tables 1 and 3 (no sentence names his variant type). Zygosity \"mosaic\" comes from the sentence naming all three patients (\"had mosaic variants in TNFAIP3\"); the paper never states germline vs somatic for them and does not report testing of their parents. disease_label_as_stated uses the Table 3 \"Clin. Pheno\" cell verbatim (LYM / DYS / DEF) plus the table-note expansion; these patients are not given an HA20 diagnosis by the authors. Table 1's \"Age\" column is not defined in the paper; it was recorded as age at last evaluation and may instead be age at sampling. clinical_diagnosis_basis left \"not reported\": the paper does not describe a diagnostic work-up for these patients. No cell in this paper contains the stacked \" / \" separator. Contradictions: Table 3 gives different primary clinical-phenotype categories (LYM for 66, DYS for 99, DEF for 507) while the text says all three had lymphoproliferation as their main symptom; both were kept, the text statement was used for the phenotype row and the table cell for the disease label. Clinical detail for these patients (for example Supplemental Table S5, cited for other patients) is in an unavailable supplement, so their other checklist items are \"not reported\".",
